' Runtime test for bug-546's second defect: a FAILED `thread::transfer` of a
' user-declared `RESOURCE … THREAD_SENDABLE` must leave the sender's handle open
' and usable. This is the user-resource twin of
' `tests/rt-behavior/threads/thread-resource-transfer-fail-leak`, which pins the
' same contract for the built-in `fs::File`.
'
' `mfb man thread transfer` states the guarantee:
'
'   If the transfer fails, the sending binding is still open, so a `TRAP` handler
'   can close it or try again.
'
' bug-425 implemented it by DEFERRING the `moved|closed` store on the sender's
' record from copy time to the enqueue-success branch. Its gate asked
' `builtins::is_thread_sendable_resource_type` — the built-in registry — so the
' deferral never applied to a resource the program declares. The flag was stored
' at copy time regardless of the outcome, and the first use in the TRAP handler
' died with `7-703-0009 ErrResourceMoved`, exit 255. That is the same builtin-only
' blind spot as bug-546's headline failure, one predicate over.
'
' The handler READS the handle before closing it — an `INSERT` into the table this
' iteration created — so a tombstoned record cannot pass: `sqlite3_exec` on a
' closed/moved binding is refused before it reaches sqlite. That also defeats a
' "make close a no-op" wrong fix, which would leave the read failing.
'
' The worker blocks on the message channel and never accepts, so the parent's
' cap-1 outbound resource queue stays full after the one fill transfer. Every
' later `transfer(t, f, 0)` then fails immediately with ErrTimeout, which is what
' makes all 50 iterations take the failure path.
IMPORT io
IMPORT thread

RESOURCE Db CLOSE BY sql::close THREAD_SENDABLE

LINK "sqlite3" AS sql
  FUNC open(path AS String) AS RES Db
    SYMBOL "sqlite3_open"
    ABI (path CString, db OUT CPtr) AS status CInt32
    RETURN db
    SUCCESS_ON status = 0
  END FUNC
  FUNC exec(RES db AS Db, statement AS String) AS Nothing
    SYMBOL "sqlite3_exec"
    ABI (db CPtr, statement CString, callback CPtr, arg CPtr, errmsg CPtr) AS status CInt32
    CONST callback = NOTHING
    CONST arg = NOTHING
    CONST errmsg = NOTHING
    SUCCESS_ON status = 0
  END FUNC
  FUNC close(RES db AS Db) AS Nothing
    SYMBOL "sqlite3_close"
    ABI (db CPtr) AS status CInt32
    SUCCESS_ON status = 0
  END FUNC
END LINK

ISOLATED FUNC blockNeverAccept(t AS ThreadWorker OF String RES Db TO Integer, seed AS String) AS Integer
  LET s AS String = thread::receive(t, 60000)
  RETURN 0
END FUNC

FUNC main AS Integer
  LET t AS Thread OF String RES Db TO Integer = thread::start(blockNeverAccept, "seed", 1, 1)
  RES fill AS Db = sql::open(":memory:")
  thread::transfer(t, fill, 1000)

  MUT closed AS Integer = 0
  MUT i AS Integer = 0
  WHILE i < 50
    RES f AS Db = sql::open(":memory:")
    sql::exec(f, "CREATE TABLE seeded(a INTEGER);")
    thread::transfer(t, f, 0) TRAP(err)
      sql::exec(f, "INSERT INTO seeded VALUES (1);")
      sql::close(f)
      closed = closed + 1
      RECOVER
    END TRAP
    i = i + 1
  END WHILE
  io::print("closed=" & toString(closed))
  RETURN 0
END FUNC
